        <headline>Small Craft Advisory issued September 25 at 3:33PM AKDT until September 26 at 5:00PM AKDT by NWS Juneau AK</headline>
        <description>Southeast Alaska Coastal Waters from Dixon Entrance to
Cape Suckling out 100 NM

Wind forecasts reflect the predominant speed and direction
expected. Seas forecasts represent the average of the highest
one-third of the combined windwave and swell height.

.TONIGHT...W wind 10 kt becoming S in the evening, then
increasing to 25 kt late. Seas 5 ft building to 8 ft late. Rain
late.
.SAT...S wind 25 kt becoming SW 15 kt in the afternoon. Seas
9 ft. Rain in the morning.
.SAT NIGHT...S wind 20 kt. Seas 9 ft. Rain in the evening.
.SUN...S wind 25 kt. Seas 11 ft. Rain.
.SUN NIGHT...S wind 25 kt. Seas 12 ft. Showers.
.MON...SW wind 20 kt. Seas 11 ft.
.TUE...W wind 20 kt. Seas 10 ft.
.WED...SW wind 20 kt. Seas 10 ft.
</description>
